Aether: telemetry backends out

Extension telemetry API, payload flows, ASRouter, client env, targeting, clientID, environment readers, reporting policy, experiment mirror, restored backends, util readers, backend JS, orphan enums.

Squashed from 14 units:

  [core/50-ext-telemetry-api.patch]
  Aether: remove the browser.telemetry WebExtension API
  
  The browser.telemetry WebExtension API only forwarded to the legacy
  backend: submitPing/canUpload reached TelemetryController, every other
  method was already a documented no-op. With no uploader and no backend
  consumers left, the whole surface goes: the parent implementation, its
  schema, the API registration and both packaging entries.
  
  [core/51-dead-payload-flows.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead telemetry payload flows
  
  Three telemetry-only data flows with no remaining readers:
  
  - XPIProvider.addAddonsToCrashReporter only fed the addon list into
    TelemetrySession (its crash-reporter half was already gone), so the
    method, its three call sites and the now-unused import go with it.
  - TelemetryTimestamps collected startup markers solely for ping payloads:
    the module, its moz.build entry, the BrowserGlue marker call and the
    payload-assembly consumer in TelemetrySession go too, along with the
    already-emptied _firstWindowTelemetry hook and its call.
  
  [core/52-asrouter-telemetry-flow.patch]
  Aether: remove the ASRouter messaging-telemetry flow
  
  The ASRouter messaging-telemetry flow ended in a hollow sink: every
  surface built ping objects that went nowhere. The whole chain goes:
  the ASRouterTelemetry module itself, the sendTelemetry threading
  (DefaultConfig, NewTabHook, ASRouter init, both Hub inits, storage
  error-reporting opt), the TELEMETRY message cases in the parent
  message handler plus the undesired/targeting-error/action-only sends
  in ASRouter core, the per-surface send sites (all nine hubs keep
  impressions, capping, actions and UI behavior), the NewTabMessaging
  forwarder (IMPRESSION dispatch kept), the content-src helper, and the
  now-orphaned message-type constants. The committed admin bundle keeps
  its copy (generated artifact); its telemetry button now hits the
  removed route. panelUI's recordMenuMessageTelemetry call stays as a
  no-op stub so the external caller is safe.
  
  [core/53-clientenv-teleportals.patch]
  Aether: remove the ClientEnvironment telemetry portals
  
  ClientEnvironment's telemetry and liveTelemetry getters exposed
  archived and live ping contents to targeting expressions, but nothing
  reads them anymore. They go along with the now-unused backend imports,
  plus a stale comment pointing at the controller for client-id caching.
  
  [core/54-targeting-attrs.patch]
  Aether: rebuild the telemetry-backed targeting attributes locally
  
  ASRouterTargeting read two telemetry-backed targeting attributes: the
  session subsession counter (profileRestartCount, used by no local
  message) and the update-settings snapshot (browserSettings). The
  counter goes away with its reader; the update snapshot is rebuilt
  from the same live sources (update channel, updater state, the two
  update prefs), so targeting sees identical values without touching
  the environment backend.
  
  [core/55-dead-clientid-import.patch]
  Aether: remove the dead ClientID import in DoHController
  
  DoHController imported ClientID but never used it. One line.
  
  [core/56-clientid-replacement.patch]
  Aether: replace ClientID with direct pref reads
  
  ClientID.sys.mjs was a pref-backed UUID store with no remaining
  telemetry purpose: every consumer only needs stable IDs. Each one now
  reads and writes the same prefs directly, so existing profiles keep
  their IDs byte-identical (backups restore, enrollments stay bucketed):
  BackupService and normandyAddonStudy take the install ID, Nimbus and
  ASRouterTargeting the profile-group ID, Discovery and the addon
  reporters the sha256 client hash (same digest), SelectableProfileService
  writes the group prefs with the same validation. UsageReporting only
  managed those IDs plus a one-time pref migration, so it goes too with
  its moz.build entries, the migration inlined into ProfileDataUpgrader.
  Unused imports (DoH went earlier, TargetingContextRecorder here) removed.
  
  [core/57-environment-readers.patch]
  Aether: cut the TelemetryEnvironment readers over to local sources
  
  Three more readers of TelemetryEnvironment go local: QuickSuggest
  drops its wait on environment init (it only fed ping payloads),
  Targeting's channel attribute reads the same default-branch pref with
  the same build fallback, browser.js drops its unused import, and the
  devtools osNameAndVersion label reads sysinfo directly. The writers
  (Nimbus/Normandy experiment state) move with their own unit.
  
  [core/58-reporting-policy.patch]
  Aether: remove the reporting-policy and ToU machinery
  
  Remote Suggest is pinned off in Aether (quicksuggest disabled, Merino
  endpoints empty), so its Terms-of-Use consent machinery has nothing to
  gate: suggestions are local-only. The whole ReportingPolicy module goes
  (data notice plus ToU), and its five consumers drop their hooks:
  BrowserGlue skips the first-run notice wait, QuickSuggest treats ToU as
  never accepted (online Suggest stays off) and drops the pref listener,
  UrlbarPrefs drops the ToU date default, PreonboardingSplash decides on
  about:welcome alone, and AboutNewTab continues initialization directly
  instead of waiting on the acceptance topic that will never fire.
  
  [core/59-experiment-env-mirror.patch]
  Aether: drop the experiment-state mirror into TelemetryEnvironment
  
  Experiment enrollment mirrored its state into TelemetryEnvironment
  alongside the live FOG calls. The legacy half goes from all five
  writers (Nimbus enrollment telemetry, addon rollouts, addon studies,
  preference experiments and rollouts) while the FOG calls and all
  enrollment logic stay untouched.
  
  [core/60-restore-backend-modules.patch]
  Aether: restore the backend-only telemetry modules
  
  Patches 56/58 deleted ClientID, UsageReporting and ReportingPolicy
  while backend modules (ControllerParent, Send, Session) still import
  them, which breaks startup with a missing-module error. The consumer
  migrations in those patches stand; the three modules come back as
  backend-only until the backend unit removes them together with their
  remaining importers.
  
  [core/61-util-readers.patch]
  Aether: cut the last TelemetryUtils and UpdatePing readers over
  
  Four more readers cut over to local sources: BrowserContentHandler
  drops the update-success ping (plus its shutdown blockers and the now
  unused AsyncShutdown import), SelectableProfileService compares against
  the canary group ID literal, FirefoxRelay generates its own flow UUID,
  and AddonManager drops an unused import. TelemetryUtils and UpdatePing
  have no product importers left.
  
  [core/62-backend-js.patch]
  Aether: delete the legacy telemetry JS backend
  
  With no product importers left, the whole legacy JS backend goes
  in one cut: all app/ controllers and helpers, all pings, the startup
  hook and its two registrations (XPCOM manifest and .manifest
  category), and every packaging entry. The C++ core, the YAML tables
  and their generators follow in the next units; the UntrustedModules
  family stays for about:thirdparty.
  
  [core/63-orphan-enum-includes.patch]
  Aether: remove the orphaned telemetry enum includes
  
  Seven files still included the generated histogram/scalar enum
  headers without using a single ID from them, leftovers from
  recording calls removed by earlier patches. One line each.
